date-released: 2026-08-09
version: v1.6.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21719868
# Zenodo mints a version DOI only when a release is published, and the identifier
# it issues cannot be predicted, so the entry for the release named above is added
# in the first commit after that release. Until then this list ends at the previous
# version. The concept DOI is what the `doi` field carries, and it never changes.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21719868
    description: >-
      Concept DOI. Represents every version of this work and always resolves to
      the most recent one. Cite this unless you need to pin a specific version.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21855599
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.6.1, the current release. It completes the corrections
      begun in v1.6.0, removing three residual assertions that consistency is
      settled and an orphaned paragraph citing the uniform law as available, and
      adds a check requiring every number in a manuscript table to be the
      correct rounding of a generated value.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21850110
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.6.0, superseded by defect. Its corrections are sound
      but incompletely applied: having labelled the location-model consistency
      corollary conditional, it still asserts in three places that consistency
      is settled, and carries an orphaned paragraph citing the uniform law as
      available. Its contribution list also still states the score-level rate
      as a necessary condition after the corollary establishing it was
      downgraded. A reader could take either side of the contradiction.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21848464
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.5.0, superseded by defect. Its uniform law of large
      numbers for the nearest-atom criterion is labelled proved, but the proof
      controls the supremum over theta of an expected empirical tail where it
      needs the expectation of the supremum, so the location-model consistency
      corollary that depends on it is not established either. v1.5.0 also
      describes the score and curvature results as concerning the simulated
      score, when they concern the nearest-atom proxy criterion, whose relation
      to the log likelihood is through criterion values rather than
      derivatives. The exact score moment and the curvature identity themselves
      are unaffected and were confirmed by external review.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21834941
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.4.0, superseded by defect. It introduces the uniform
      law of large numbers whose proof v1.6.0 corrects, and states the
      location-model consistency corollary as proved; both are conditional on an
      empirical-tail hypothesis that v1.4.0 does not verify. Its correction of
      the rate condition misreported in v1.3.0 stands.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21830098
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.3.0, superseded. Its remark on the uniform-in-theta
      step asserts that the step plausibly requires N >> S^(2/K) and that this
      points the opposite way to the published rate conditions. Both are wrong:
      the chaining bound was taken over the metric diameter of the index set
      rather than over the envelope of the function class, and the correct
      condition, N >> log S, is compatible with those conditions. No result in
      v1.3.0 depends on the claim, which described an open step rather than
      serving as a hypothesis.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21823961
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.2.0, superseded by v1.3.0, which closes two problems
      v1.2.0 records as open: the logarithmic gap in the subcritical collapse
      theorem, and the dependence of the scaling law on assumption (A5).
      Nothing in v1.2.0 is known to be wrong; its results are weaker.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21763715
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.1.0, superseded by v1.2.0. Nothing in it is known to be
      wrong; it is simply the single-document form.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21760062
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.0.3, superseded by v1.1.0. Its Proposition 3.1 gives the
      critical case without the limit law, and its Section 6 states the score
      result conditionally.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21729471
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.0.2, superseded. Its Proposition E.2 omits the
      hypothesis |rho_ww*| <= 1 and is false as a standalone statement.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21728285
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.0.1, superseded. Its Remark E.6 wrongly calls a
      magnitude condition vacuous.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21719869
    description: >-
      Version DOI for v1.0.0, superseded. It states the limit in Proposition C.1
      in the wrong direction.
